{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals","id":1407869,"title":"Martial Arts and Alchemicals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-12T23:55:38-07:00","id":1407869,"title":"Martial Arts and Alchemicals","content":"Alchemicals have a singuler weakness--they cannot use all their charms, and the more charms they pack, the more essence is committed. <br /> <br /> Martial arts, are thus a logical choice, since for the cost of one &quot;installed&quot; charm you can get lots of other charms.<br /> <br /> But it struck me, at their core, exalted martial arts are a different way of manipulating essence. Wouldn't alchemical be interested in adapting this for other purposes? IE, adapting the style of martial arts to other purposes, so as to get around that problem with installed charms? I mean, after over 5,000 years in the Great Maker, I'd have to assume someone considered it and Autocthon is pretty much all <i>about</i> adapting and making tools to extend your own abilities...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:00:41-07:00","id":1407887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals#post1407869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it struck me, at their core, exalted martial arts are a different way of manipulating essence. Wouldn't alchemical be interested in adapting this for other purposes? IE, adapting the style of martial arts to other purposes, so as to get around that problem with installed charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be what Martial Arts are at their core, but that doesn't mean they can be reduced down from fighting styles that allow one's Essence to emulate other forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, after over 5,000 years in the Great Maker, I'd have to assume someone considered it and Autocthon is pretty much all <i>about</i> adapting and making tools to extend your own abilities...</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time ago I came to think about how the most sensible way to look at the Alchemical Exalted is not as Autochthon in miniature, but how Autochthon would create heroes.<br /> <br /> As in, he'd literally create them. And they would be heroes for his purposes of defending the survival of humanity within his hostile reaches. But they would not be like him.<br /> <br /> Much like how I presume the Dragon-Blooded more reflect the conception of heroism held by the Elemental Dragons than they do the Dragons themselves.<br /> <br /> Still, sure society in Autochthonia in general draws what it can to pursue useful iterations. I could imagine some Sodalts wondering if Alchemicals could develop other forms of power along similar principles. But I don't imagine they'd get very far even without the restrictions of Alchemicals with a wide array of powers not dependent on returning to the vats being contrary to the interests of the Nations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T08:56:55-07:00","id":1407957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals#post1407869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts, are thus a logical choice, </div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern weaving/spells is the other notable way for Alchemicals to expand their capacity for magic, note.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it struck me, at their core, exalted martial arts are a different way of manipulating essence. Wouldn't alchemical be interested in adapting this for other purposes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. The fact that, in ~4000 years of Alchemicals thinking about the issue, they haven't yet managed to find a way to do so probably indicates that it's not really something that can be done, though. It's much like the design advice for custom charms - designing a charm that's &quot;Like charm X, but 2 motes cheaper&quot; isn't really kosher, because the game assumes that all the low-hanging fruit of making charms more efficient, effective, etc. has already been done. A custom charm has to do something distinctly <i>different</i>.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you were going to come up with a new way for Alchemicals to expand their powers, it should probably follow similar guidelines to how they already do it: require a basic Alchemical charm to be installed that grants access to this new powerset, and the new powerset should be fairly restricted in what it can do. Martial arts are all about combat, and each martial art style has a particular theme and structure within that larger category, and becoming good at one style doesn't necessarily let you skip steps and get good charms of other styles, you still have to build <i>them</i> up from the base too. So if you wanted to create, say, &quot;social styles&quot;, that might be possible, but you'd have to learn specifically &quot;Social Butterfly Style&quot; or &quot;Aggressive Bully Style&quot; or something, and the really potent social effects would be locked off for higher levels of skill in that style.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:00:57-07:00","id":1407958,"title":"","content":"You make a compelling argument for Alchemicals to be Terrestrial martial artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:18:06-07:00","id":1408010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals?p=1407958#post1407958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a compelling argument for Alchemicals to be Terrestrial martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be down for that, though as with DBs having the Immaculate styles, I would not be surprised if there were very very very machine-themed styles that lack the Terrestrial Keyword and are enhanced by Clarity (or Dissonance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:03:50-07:00","id":1408059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals?p=1407958#post1407958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a compelling argument for Alchemicals to be Terrestrial martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding this is actually the case in <b>Exalted Essence</b> at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:56:40-07:00","id":1408088,"title":"","content":"I have hever played an alchemical without at least one terrestrial style and perfected lotus Matrix. Sure it's a permanent commitment of 2 motes, but equally, if you grab a few styles, you're never going to be disarmed, and that's the worst danger facing an alchemical, especially if she or he is designated tech/face/skill monkey of the assembly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T03:48:31-07:00","id":1408122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1407869-martial-arts-and-alchemicals?p=1408010#post1408010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be down for that, though as with DBs having the Immaculate styles, I would not be surprised if there were very very very machine-themed styles that lack the Terrestrial Keyword and are enhanced by Clarity (or Dissonance)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that does not regard the &quot;why&quot; behind the Immaculate Styles.<br /> <br /> The basic setup of the setting including the fact that the world ruling empire hunts down the Anathema with a branch of its evil state Buddhism that employs specialised martial arts for the purpose, provided under the tutelage of the secret martial arts masters, that all seems to have appeared fairly early in development. The Immaculate Styles as they originally appeared were just the implementation of that vision, a core component of the world based on iconic literary and historical precedent and various elements in sync. The implementation in this Edition is just adjusted to account for how martial arts in general were made more accessible, and taking advantage of the central mechanical hook of the Dragon Blooded. It retains the conceit in character that it required the assistance of the Sidereals to realise them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Machine themed styles enhanced by Clarity&quot; does not seem to me to have any of that force behind it. Not the image of where these special martial artists fit and where they come from, I very much doubt that Clarity will hold much significance to their overall Charmset, and &quot;machine theme&quot; does not really carry the weight in and out of character that each Immculate Dragon does.<br /> <br /> It doesn't sound like something expressing a major element of story, just looking for mechanical parity. But it would seem unnecessary for the Alchemicals if they have so much other power in the rest of their Charms.<br /> <br /> Besides, shouldn't a special relationship with a particular set of martial arts remain an exclusive feature of the Dragon Blooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:22:15-07:00","id":1408162,"title":"","content":"What if Alchemicals were normally terrestrial restricted but could get a charm that removed it for a certain style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}